    "text": {
     "en": "Barter is exchanging goods without money. It needed a double coincidence of wants: each person had to want what the other had.\nCoins of metal like copper, silver and gold came next because they are durable and valued. Later paper notes were used.\nToday we also use digital money. The Reserve Bank of India issues our notes."
    }
